                <pb facs="0828" n="818" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg818"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.002/1130: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-10-11T19:00:00-05:00">October 11, 1941—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>241. Your 414, October 8, 10 a.m., Chinese Maritime Customs. Department concurs
                    in the views expressed in your telegram under reference and desires that the
                    American Consul General at Shanghai make to the Inspector General of Customs the
                    statement suggested in the first substantive paragraph of your telegram.</p>
                <p>Sent to Chungking, repeated to Shanghai. Shanghai repeat to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
